d segments"],[463,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1031,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1533,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1154,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[204,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[931,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[462,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1030,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[202,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[929,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[928,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[201,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[930,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[203,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1894,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[149,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[447,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[243,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[261,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[239,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[254,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1573,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1783,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1292,"`Content`, `Header`, `Footer`, and `ButtonGroup` each accept all `Flex` layout props."],[963,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[558,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[561,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[557,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[559,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[560,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[562,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1231,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[291,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[324,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[877,"`Enter/Space`"],[367,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[659,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[333,"`Escape`"],[805,"`Escape`"],[879,"`Escape`"],[1578,"`Escape`"],[402,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1816,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[566,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1854,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[618,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[647,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[676,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1766,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1900,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[702,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1899,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[737,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[147,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[294,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[800,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[796,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[962,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1626,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1364,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1568,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[667,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[650,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[871,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[653,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[906,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[911,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1017,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1785,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1786,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1784,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[807,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[881,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[337,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[565,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[564,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[200,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[927,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1027,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1151,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1026,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1150,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1532,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1531,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[743,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1454,"`size` is the tier: the eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`,\nand the body on `body`. Use `2xl` for a page title, `xl` for a hero, `lg` for a section\ntitle, and `md` (the default) everywhere else."],[617,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name."],[1898,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[45,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1257,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[964,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[43,"`Tab`"],[335,"`Tab`"],[365,"`Tab`"],[661,"`Tab`"],[803,"`Tab`"],[1576,"`Tab`"],[1368,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1365,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1369,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1367,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1399,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1459,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1085,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[781,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1567,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[1777,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[782,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[1787,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[1765,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1628,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[1770,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[1761,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[1901,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[1763,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[1771,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[1774,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[1897,"`xs`